for us.

279
00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.969
That is what this campaign has been about.

280
00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.409
Now it's going to take all of us working together

281
00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:37.169
from all political persuasions to address

282
00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:38.960
the issues that our state faces.

283
00:12:39.789 --> 00:12:42.900
But I truly believe that we can do great things for this state

284
00:12:43.159 --> 00:12:44.200
with all ideas,

285
00:12:44.309 --> 00:12:44.640
voices,

286
00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.669
and perspectives actually at the table.

287
00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.320
Politics should never,

288
00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:49.239
ever,

289
00:12:49.799 --> 00:12:50.580
ever be

290
00:12:50.929 --> 00:12:53.789
about two private clubs who are more interested in beating up

291
00:12:53.789 --> 00:12:56.140
on each other than they are in solving our problems.

292
00:13:02.979 --> 00:13:05.270
Problem solving across the aisle is something that

293
00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:07.359
you can expect from me as your governor.

294
00:13:07.869 --> 00:13:11.440
My mission is going to be to make state government work better for all Iowans,

295
00:13:11.549 --> 00:13:12.669
to serve all Iowans,

296
00:13:12.979 --> 00:13:15.530
and to be accountable to all Iowans.

297
00:13:15.989 --> 00:13:18.210
We also learned something else in this campaign.

298
00:13:18.789 --> 00:13:20.010
The lies didn't work.

299
00:13:22.169 --> 00:13:25.039
The only two fair attacks about me

300
00:13:25.219 --> 00:13:27.820
were that I can ride a skateboard and I do like pizza.

301
00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:31.500
And as Christine said,

302
00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.739
these lies were nothing compared to our loss

303
00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.210
on October 15th,

304
00:13:36.539 --> 00:13:38.280
but they're also nothing compared to the struggle that

305
00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.739
so many Iowans go through every single day,

306
00:13:41.219 --> 00:13:43.900
trying to provide for their families or play the

307
00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:46.159
difficult hand that they've been dealt in life.

308
00:13:46.739 --> 00:13:50.799
Enough Iowans know me well enough that they spread the truth to others around them

309
00:13:50.979 --> 00:13:51.969
about who I am,

310
00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:53.340
and that proved.

311
00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:55.210
That Iowa can still

312
00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:58.830
work like one big small town where being open and being honest

313
00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:00.969
is the best way to get through it all in the end.

314
00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:02.989
Here's to Iowa on that one.

315
00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.969
I do want to thank my opponent,

316
00:14:11.039 --> 00:14:12.710
Zach Lane for getting in the race.

317
00:14:12.929 --> 00:14:15.950
I said the same thing when Governor Reynolds announced her retirement.

318
00:14:16.289 --> 00:14:18.929
Public office and campaigning is a difficult thing to

319
00:14:18.929 --> 00:14:21.640
do in a way that few people truly understand.

320
00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:24.630
Putting your name out there and your ideas out there is tough.

321
00:14:25.049 --> 00:14:27.239
And I appreciated the places where we agreed.

322
00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:28.140
I'm glad

323
00:14:28.609 --> 00:14:30.950
to see someone win a Republican nomination talking

324
00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.109
about water quality and talking about cancer.

325
00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:33.929
Yeah.

326
00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:39.969
So let's use that bipartisan support from Iowa voters to actually

327
00:14:39.969 --> 00:14:43.489
get our water cleaned up and our cancer rates under control.

328
00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:53.580
Tonight Iowans across the state made their voices heard,

329
00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:57.229
and they voted to restore our public schools to their former glory.

330
00:14:57.599 --> 00:14:59.900
They voted to address our cancer crisis

331
00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:01.359
with real solutions,

332
00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:02.119
not with rhetoric,

333
00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.559
and to make public service the focus of government,

334
00:15:04.679 --> 00:15:05.719
not politics,

335
00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:07.219
by regulating,

336
00:15:07.479 --> 00:15:07.960
well,

337
00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.140
the people that need regulation the most,

338
00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:11.239
politicians.

339
00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:14.630
More than anything else,

340
00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:16.590
Iowans voted for change.

341
00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:18.539
They voted for checks and balances,

342
00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.890
and they voted to bring transparency and accountability

343
00:15:22.229 --> 00:15:24.049
back to state government.

344
00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:24.789
Now,

345
00:15:24.869 --> 00:15:26.169
to Iowa's legislators,

346
00:15:26.349 --> 00:15:27.869
I look forward to working with you

347
00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:28.729
on the same

348
00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:32.969
common sense ideas and solutions that we advocated for throughout this campaign.

349
00:15:34.049 --> 00:15:34.929
Iowans,

350
00:15:35.219 --> 00:15:36.900
including Democrats and Independents,

351
00:15:37.289 --> 00:15:38.570
voted for these issues.

352
00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:40.359
They are broadly popular,

353
00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.739
and we would all do well to pass them into reality.

354
00:15:43.979 --> 00:15:45.650
As I said on the campaign trail,

355
00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:50.450
I'm going to be spending 100% of my time addressing the concerns of 100% of Iowans,

356
00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:51.919
and you have my word,

357
00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:53.570
legislators,

358
00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:55.200
any bill you vote for

359
00:15:55.619 --> 00:15:59.500
is a bill where you are invited to the bill ceremony signing ceremony.

360
00:16:00.169 --> 00:16:02.789
That's the kind of credit given where credit is due,

361
00:16:02.849 --> 00:16:06.210
sort of common sense attitude that Iowans expect from their government.

362
00:16:07.369 --> 00:16:08.219
Thank you again.

363
00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.289
To the people of the state of Iowa for putting your trust in me

364
00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:13.590
as your next governor.

365
00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:15.489
I hope.

366
00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:22.849
And I hope

367
00:16:23.919 --> 00:16:26.179
No matter who you voted for in this race.

368
00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.250
I hope over the next week,

369
00:16:28.390 --> 00:16:31.539
you're going to go find somebody that voted differently than you

370
00:16:31.909 --> 00:16:32.969
and ask them why,

371
00:16:33.349 --> 00:16:34.070
and just listen.

372
00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:37.349
And keep asking,

373
00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:39.650
tell me more or say something else

374
00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:41.869
until they say something.

375
00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:43.650
That you agree with

376
00:16:44.659 --> 00:16:45.559
When they do that,

377
00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:46.719
Let them know.

378
00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:47.900
Will we agree on that.

379
00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:51.479
That's one thing that you can do yourself,

380
00:16:51.929 --> 00:16:55.099
everyone in the state to help rebuild the social fabric of our state,

381
00:16:55.409 --> 00:16:57.239
and remember that all of us together,

382
00:16:57.409 --> 00:16:58.130
our neighbors,

383
00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:58.989
our friends,

384
00:16:59.489 --> 00:17:00.260
we all

385
00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.150
have a job to do to make this state

386
00:17:02.609 --> 00:17:03.549
better and truer,

387
00:17:03.909 --> 00:17:05.170
not just redder and bluer.

388
00:17:05.439 --> 00:17:06.260
Let's get to work.

